# Line-ending policy.
#
# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree: a CRLF checkout makes
# `bash scripts/*.sh` fail with `$'\r': command not found`, and a Windows
# working copy is also what a local Docker build would copy into the
# containers, so the breakage is not limited to the developer's own shell.
#
# `text eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf for the matched paths, so the outcome
# no longer depends on each contributor's local Git configuration
# (github.com docs, "Configuring Git to handle line endings": a committed
# .gitattributes "overrides the core.autocrlf setting for all repository
# contributors"; gitattributes(5): the eol attribute "sets a specific
# line-ending style to be used in the working directory").
*.sh text eol=lf
